        "original_id": "657b95f0-119b-5868-b61d-6025ef02c09a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Game of the Goose, Medina, The Will of an Eccentric\n- People: Jules Verne\n- Places: Medina, Atlas Mountains\n- Concepts: board games, adventure novels\n\nFacts:\n- In 1900, Jules Verne wrote The Will of an Eccentric, an adventure novel based on the Game of the Goose.\n- The Game of the Goose is a board game in which two or more players move pieces around a track by rolling a die.\n- Medina is a board game in which three or four players compete to be the most influential developer of Medina, a desert city near the Atlas Mountains, in 1822.\n- Variations of Medina allow 2 or 5 players.",
